{"term":"damp","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:9448773970e5d47c43","definition":"In a state between dry and wet; moderately wet; moist.","example":"25 January 2017, Leena Camadoo writing in The Guardian, Dominican banana producers at sharp end of climate change\nOnce the farms have been drained and the dead plants have been cut down and cleared, farmers then have to be alert for signs of black sigatoka, a devastating fungus which flourishes in damp conditions and can destroy banana farms.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["moist"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bedamp","damp-dry","dampen","damp haze","dampish","damply","dampness","dampsome","damp squib","damp squid","dampth","dampy","damp down","damp off"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damp#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9ffd69dfaa032f15cc","definition":"Despondent; dispirited, downcast.","example":"27 July 2016, Jane O’Faherty in The Irish Independent, Monarchs and prison officers win big on second race day\nThough Travis's 'Why does it always Rain on Me' boomed around the stands, there were few damp spirits in Galway on day two of the races.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["glum"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["bedamp","damp-dry","dampen","damp haze","dampish","damply","dampness","dampsome","damp squib","damp squid","dampth","dampy","damp down","damp off"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damp#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e99b1bf93302531303","definition":"Permitting the possession of alcoholic beverages, but not their sale.","example":"The Roadhouse was twenty-seve miles down the road from Niniltna, nine feet and three inches outside the Niniltna Native Association's tribal jurisdiction, and therefore not subject to the dry law currently in effect. Or was it damp? Kate thought it might have changed, yet again, at the last election, from dry to damp, or maybe it was from wet to damp.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["thoan","thone","melancholy","sorrowful"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bedamp","damp-dry","dampen","damp haze","dampish","damply","dampness","dampsome","damp squib","damp squid","dampth","dampy","damp down","damp off"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damp#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:25fff89124c5788219","definition":"Moisture; humidity; dampness.","example":"Ere twice in murk and occidental damp / Moist Hesperus hath quench’d his sleepy lamp,","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["bedamp","damp-dry","dampen","damp haze","dampish","damply","dampness","dampsome","damp squib","damp squid","dampth","dampy","damp down","damp off","afterdamp","blackdamp","chokedamp","choke damp","damp course","dampless","dampproof","damp-proof course","damp proofing","damp sheet","death-damp","firedamp","flashdamp","rising damp","stinkdamp","whitedamp"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damp#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:daa2a2a9afb9d34182","definition":"Fog; fogginess; vapor.","example":"Night […] with black air / Accompanied, with damps and dreadful gloom.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["bedamp","damp-dry","dampen","damp haze","dampish","damply","dampness","dampsome","damp squib","damp squid","dampth","dampy","damp down","damp off","afterdamp","blackdamp","chokedamp","choke damp","damp course","dam